de me sad.","speakerId":"Ntt_DC270F89","textSource":"localization","pronounText":{"TextHeVersion":"This made me sad.","TextSheVersion":"~","TextTheyVersion":"~"},"effects":[],"conditions":[],"script":"","demeanor":null,"position":{"x":2200.0,"y":650.0},"source":{"file":"resources.assets","pathId":"28565","byteOffset":18691888,"byteLength":336}},{"id":"DFr_14158F5C","articyId":"72057615512868358","type":"choice","className":"DialogueFragment","speaker":"Player","text":"Me too.","speakerId":"Ntt_4A96A8B1","textSource":"localization","pronounText":{"TextHeVersion":"Me too.","TextSheVersion":"Me too.","TextTheyVersion":"Me too."},"effects":[],"conditions":[],"script":"","demeanor":null,"position":{"x":2500.0,"y":775.0},"source":{"file":"resources.assets","pathId":"21788","byteOffset":16132600,"byteLength":288}},{"id":"DFr_451B70B4","articyId":"72057615512868371","type":"line","className":"DialogueFragment","speaker":"DeeDee","text":"My Dearest Huckleberry,\r\n\r\nAs I sit here, my heart aches with the memories of our rail-riding days. Time has aged me, tethering me to this place, while you continue your endless journey, searching for a way to forget what happened.","speakerId":"Ntt_F290F0AE","textSource":"localization","pronounText":{"TextHeVersion":"My Dearest Huckleberry,\r\n\r\nAs I sit here, my heart aches with the memories of our rail-riding days. Time has aged me, tethering me to this place, while you continue your endless journey, searching for a way to forget what happened.","TextSheVersion":"~","TextTheyVersion":"~"},"effects":[],"conditions":[],"script":"","demeanor":null,"position":{"x":1400.0,"y":775.0},"source":{"file":"resources.assets","pathId":"46276","byteOffset":31837976,"byteLength":524}},{"id":"DFr_E309FD71","articyId":"72057615512868751","type":"line","className":"DialogueFragment","speaker":"Ava","text":"Do you think Huckleberry will change his mind?","speakerId":"Ntt_DC270F89","textSource":"localization","pronounText":{"TextHeVersion":"Do you think Huckleberry will change his mind?","TextSheVersion":"~","TextTheyVersion":"~"},"effects":[],"conditions":[],"script":"","demeanor":null,"position":{"x":2800.0,"y":775.0},"source":{"file":"resources.assets","pathId":"32985","byteOffset":20363712,"byteLength":328}},{"id":"DFr_4F843956","articyId":"72057615512868758","type":"choice","className":"DialogueFragment","speaker":"Player","text":"I'm not sure, but we should definitely not call him Huckleberry.","speakerId":"Ntt_4A96A8B1","textSource":"localization","pronounText":{"TextHeVersion":"I'm not sure, but we should definitely not call him Huckleberry.","TextSheVersion":"I'm not sure, but we should definitely not call him Huckleberry.","TextTheyVersion":"I'm not sure, but we should definitely not call him Huckleberry."},"effects":[],"conditions":[],"script":"","demeanor":null,"position":{"x":3075.0,"y":775.0},"source":{"file":"resources.assets","pathId":"18344","byteOffset":14828184,"byteLength":344}},{"id":"DFr_C9D86B62","articyId":"72057615512909423","type":"choice","className":"DialogueFragment","speaker":"Player","text":"It's not really our problem.","speakerId":"Ntt_4A96A8B1","textSource":"localization","pronounText":{"TextHeVersion":"It's not really our problem.","TextSheVersion":"It's not really our problem.","TextTheyVersion":"It's not really our problem."},"effects":[],"conditions":[],"script":"","demeanor":null,"position":{"x":2500.0,"y":550.0},"source":{"file":"resources.assets","pathId":"38428","byteOffset":28872264,"byteLength":308}},{"id":"DFr_53239145","articyId":"72057606922845704","type":"line","className":"DialogueFragment","speaker":"DeeDee","text":"I often wonder where you are, what stories you've collected, and the new friendships you've made. Catching the last wind at the bottom of a train wagon is not how I want to leave this world. Until the tracks lead you here, we are destined to move in different directions. And maybe that's ok. \r\n\r\nYours always,\r\n\r\nDeandra.","speakerId":"Ntt_F290F